invariant: INV-50
file: sha512_compress_blocks.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh sha512_compress_blocks
reason: load_block reads the block's last word one byte late, so it reads
  the byte after the block: the first byte of the next block, or, for a
  message's last block, a byte past the caller's buffer. Every digest is
  wrong too, but the read is the finding a digest cannot show. The
  harness runs the function on arrays of exactly one and exactly two
  blocks, and its bounds check fails on the read past each.

--- old
    ring[15] = load_word(p + 120);
--- new
    ring[15] = load_word(p + 121);
